roblem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $$\n\\displaystyle {\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$” is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=(-1)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is false. For example, the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ can't be written as a linear combination of \n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$\n\nsince all these linear combinations result in matrices with the entry ${a}_{22}=0:$\n\n$$\na\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+b\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+c\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 6b \\\\ -2c & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$$\n\\displaystyle {\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$”; “$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $$\n\\displaystyle {\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360523 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c860248f-2167-58c8-87fa-5053ba205a13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452167} {:answer/id #uuid "28fe9ba6-8189-5224-bf66-47ad63b7bfad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28fe9ba6-8189-5224-bf66-47ad63b7bfad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452168} :answer-field/id #uuid "06c3b965-56bb-5af4-b2ab-93b39a35d64b" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452931} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88afd962-6b15-5245-88e9-243e062057b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452169} {:answer/id #uuid "c4197e6b-54ce-5ade-90d9-6328e5f4cd64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4197e6b-54ce-5ade-90d9-6328e5f4cd64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452170} :answer-field/id #uuid "59b54ffc-e9ac-58a8-b1a8-a4ab9361e15c" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452932} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db6df491-5fe1-5fe6-a1b3-064e0e51ac82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452171} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c17006-ca48-5392-8bef-d97644e75c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5c17006-ca48-5392-8bef-d97644e75c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452172} :answer-field/id #uuid "94a15b92-9c3a-50c1-9d95-1e6a32a695cc" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e6efc92-73ea-52ca-ba80-456c38800684" :question/math-academy-id "q-94870" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{4}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$” is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+(-5)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+8\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true. Indeed, the set is linearly independent and for any matrix in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}=a\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+b\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+c\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+d\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$”; “$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$”; “$$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1eeb868-67f8-5e90-bcd7-a4c218ddaf6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452173} {:answer/id #uuid "7b350d13-391f-5c5c-a2d2-4bb4d0254262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1eeb868-67f8-5e90-bcd7-a4c218ddaf6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452173} :answer-field/id #uuid "96ed034f-1c30-5a27-8688-94e66209a2fc" :answer-field/key "${{b}_{1},{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}}$ is a basis of $V$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452934} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fdad5bf-b8a5-5dda-b143-6942f346fae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452175} {:answer/id #uuid "3f204a84-b98f-5730-9690-adad3004b57d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f204a84-b98f-5730-9690-adad3004b57d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452176} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa5a8313-7561-5b75-8bf0-24c9ae0c0861" :answer-field/key "${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},w}$ is linearly dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452935} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ec944d-a5cd-5a12-bdb4-892b18ae8eb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452177} {:answer/id #uuid "0aabb70c-b0d8-5ea1-8fbb-2e1baca1eadd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aabb70c-b0d8-5ea1-8fbb-2e1baca1eadd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452178} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4991c3a-8721-5b8f-af1c-62de8228a234" :answer-field/key "${{b}_{1},{b}_{3}}$ is linearly independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452936}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "592ff49d-bbdc-5145-a575-8c4e0989eb45" :question/math-academy-id "q-94943" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of a vector space $V.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ is a basis, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ is a maximally linearly independent set of vectors in $V,$ and\n\n- $B$ spans $V.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “${{b}_{1},{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}}$ is a basis of $V$” is false since the vector ${b}_{3}$ can't be written as a linear combination of ${{b}_{1},{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}}.$ But then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{3} & ={x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}({b}_{1}-{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){b}_{1}+(-{x}_{2}){b}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that $B$ is linearly dependent. This would contradict the fact that $B$ is a basis.\n\n- Statement “${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},w}$ is linearly dependent” is true. Since $B$ is a basis of $V,$ it is a maximally linearly independent set of vectors. This means that if we add any new vector to the set, it becomes linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${{b}_{1},{b}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Indeed, if ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent then there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwhere at least one of $x$'s is not zero. But then \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+0{b}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that $B$ is linearly dependent. This would contradict the fact that $B$ is a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},w}$ is linearly dependent”; “${{b}_{1},{b}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363384 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9815692-a138-50b9-b4b5-53d1deb36416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451341} {:answer/id #uuid "13928f2f-cd46-56fa-8c97-9a173d41a9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13928f2f-cd46-56fa-8c97-9a173d41a9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451342} :answer-field/id #uuid "66207179-6782-51a7-8c9c-26b58946b0d4" :answer-field/key "$5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452518} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bb7403c-1de8-5af0-a703-e840aa64edc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451343} {:answer/id #uuid "258dfd42-9353-508c-8008-3bf0dbe86ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bb7403c-1de8-5af0-a703-e840aa64edc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451343} :answer-field/id #uuid "95bc3e49-a85f-5996-a916-5f5842714a44" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452519} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ba72e82-49bf-51a3-b88b-521926f583b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451345} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc155c3-cd22-58ba-9542-04ba60e1df40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcc155c3-cd22-58ba-9542-04ba60e1df40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451346} :answer-field/id #uuid "9358e9ed-4724-59aa-b3e0-47a55115aa88" :answer-field/key "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cd19f076-6276-574d-a171-58c6f862f950" :question/math-academy-id "q-157239" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =5\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5-2-3 \\\\ -10+1+9 \\\\ -5-1+6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false. Since statement $5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=5,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$; “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1c26475-90bd-5e7a-84b3-47ac0bd01588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367937} {:answer/id #uuid "97a92173-cc7b-5847-916b-da911b96d3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367938} {:answer/id #uuid "3f69175b-4c5a-5019-855c-5dd66c050c76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367939} {:answer/id #uuid "135066fa-e5ab-531e-823d-7b8a43cfbd6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367940} {:answer/id #uuid "f54d27f3-bd4c-5652-a2f5-cdb2aeecffce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97a92173-cc7b-5847-916b-da911b96d3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367938} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ee53708-7bbe-5275-be3b-4ffaa95c115d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367936}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8557cbac-c9fb-5ae6-8b4f-ab9d7e2cdf03" :question/math-academy-id "q-20515" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z &=-4 \\\\ 2x+5y+3z &=-10 \\\\ 3x+6y+4z &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e289daf-4c28-5e8b-b06d-9bfb29306c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,-12,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368704} {:answer/id #uuid "de191ec5-6dfc-5619-92ef-3ef733d0d523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,-9,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368705} {:answer/id #uuid "22b06387-1b81-5688-bd9a-ca492425a4e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,-6,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368706} {:answer/id #uuid "c999c0cc-98fe-58fa-aacd-b8e42f127e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,-3,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368707} {:answer/id #uuid "52fa9cba-0e91-5d16-a4da-3d9fa8b32a91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,-15,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22b06387-1b81-5688-bd9a-ca492425a4e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,-6,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368706} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e1e8500-0044-5eb8-b6ac-7951b743cc1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "38fec071-dd2c-5be5-8833-47ebc39dc16e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73569" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 3 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 3 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=1 \\\\ y-3z &=-9 \\\\ z &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-3(1)=-9\\,⟹\\,y=-6.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-6$ and $z=1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-(-6)+2(1)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-7,y=-6$, and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-7,-6,1⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9341f62-c8f8-570d-80c8-63278f533fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13$, $y=4$, and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368711} {:answer/id #uuid "cf00639b-8c94-5353-94da-3f2b856bf365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368712} {:answer/id #uuid "48282e37-d5c2-509a-8252-6ee2a8e03b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368713} {:answer/id #uuid "3baa2212-ba77-51f2-be2f-5e043a5564f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=10$, $y=3$, and $z=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368714} {:answer/id #uuid "da3d5251-f525-5757-9a3a-816f522e1513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=16$, $y=5$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48282e37-d5c2-509a-8252-6ee2a8e03b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368713} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc8d2c28-de03-52ea-8fb5-2bfbbb958a9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3f809106-1e50-5a91-813a-0a376c6d5c21" :question/math-academy-id "q-73587" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=1 \\\\ y-z &=-4 \\\\ z &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(1) &=-4\\,⟹\\,y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3(-3) &=1\\,⟹\\,x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1.$"}]}
